# Recorded corpus captures are byte snapshots, not editable source: a case-set
# manifest under corpus/case-sets pins a SHA-256 over the exact bytes of each
# case.json and change.diff, so any checkout that rewrites line endings breaks
# that pin. core.autocrlf=true is the Git for Windows default, which is how a
# Windows checkout silently produced CRLF bytes and failed the digest. Mark the
# tree binary so Git never converts it in either direction.
corpus/** -text
corpus/seeds/**/change.diff whitespace=-space-before-tab
